  "notes": "OK-TSO (c/n 35793), the jet measured, became HA-TSO with Smartwings Hungary in late 2025 and keeps the scheme. On Eurowings wet-leases (2025) it flew with the fuselage sweep covered and Eurowings titles; not drawn. The winglets' art (the fin's spikes again) is only sketched: low. The fin's stripes and loop were traced by color on the left photo and match the right side's mirrored. The title and its mark sit on the same stretch on both sides, read from each side's own aft end. Two blues: the fin tip is a darker navy than the royal blue of the spikes, band and titles, on both sides in the same light.",
  "history": "Smartwings (Travel Service until 2019) has worn this scheme on its 737s since the 2010s."
}
